  "k1_context": "Regime differs from the organizers' observed bottleneck. Their load test (ashby-hackathon-2026/CLAUDE.md, 'Load test, 2026-10-16': CONCH behind the hosted model server on one A40, about 65 images/s) found the limit was per-image CPU preprocessing inside the single uvicorn event loop (serve.py adapter.preprocess in the request handler), not the GPU. This benchmark is a batched (16), GPU-forward-bound pipeline on an RTX 5060 with CONCH in fp32, where preprocessing is only 9.5% of the reference run, hence x1.11 end to end. The preprocessing speedup itself is x202; on faster GPUs (shorter forward passes) or in per-image serving (preprocessing in the request path) the preprocessing share, and so K1's end-to-end effect, differs. Those regimes were not measured here.",
